      "pdfPages": [
        93
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 2,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0055",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s02-p093-01140-s003",
      "sentenceText": "Somehow, all four members of the Kim family start working for the Park family and discover the life of the rich.",
      "sentenceSha256": "7ec2b1250ecdc555d73e77f7b2057fc548099fb17c6faa769ef429b2163f73e0",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s02-p093-01140-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-027",
      "parentFingerprint": "7658d5d6ac9282e8ed6b6ec8b4340597b5ae7aa98b1a2d0b13c19d0fbace31c2",
      "passageSha256": "d2b7a4d03a251d915717b6fc0d2d79fba09d3485dffc15c8ce68a007611a4ca6",
      "pdfPages": [
        93
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 3,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0056",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s02-p093-01140-s006",
      "sentenceText": "On the other hand, contrary to the stereotypes that portray the rich as savvy and calculating, the Parks are nice and naive.",
      "sentenceSha256": "8c5d9a0a9168ff7fccad317955d033e121095acafac8b7f896fc08ab08e4a221",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s02-p093-01140-r005-008",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-028",
      "parentFingerprint": "d38d6134da69e11423d9eae887e9375adb4b9ce2d9addce1d1fa260419f79866",
      "passageSha256": "d8382f712dfe1202599260b8d081207933639716c7180e5369f86296747b49d0",
      "pdfPages": [
        93
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 4,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0057",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s02-p093-01140-s007",
      "sentenceText": "In a memorable scene, Mr. Kim describes Ms. Park, saying, “She’s rich, but still nice.”",
      "sentenceSha256": "8f014fbbbe8ce6edcfc6d0e8c5970e371bf8fe0494cf0ca4671282218d85f6fb",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s02-p093-01140-r005-008",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-028",
      "parentFingerprint": "d38d6134da69e11423d9eae887e9375adb4b9ce2d9addce1d1fa260419f79866",
      "passageSha256": "d8382f712dfe1202599260b8d081207933639716c7180e5369f86296747b49d0",
      "pdfPages": [
        93
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 5,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0058",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s02-p093-01140-s008",
      "sentenceText": "Ms. Kim replies, “Not ‘rich, but still nice.’",
      "sentenceSha256": "634b231807fbf9966ec1d6af50847d1c93128d045075111886d7aaea875cbb6b",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s02-p093-01140-r005-008",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-028",
      "parentFingerprint": "d38d6134da69e11423d9eae887e9375adb4b9ce2d9addce1d1fa260419f79866",
      "passageSha256": "d8382f712dfe1202599260b8d081207933639716c7180e5369f86296747b49d0",
      "pdfPages": [
        93
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 6,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0059",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s02-p093-01140-s009",
      "sentenceText": "She’s nice because she’s rich.",
      "sentenceSha256": "a95bf2a5fb66f247baf04c03e10ebd449e942290e49cb24898e3e5090e966601",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s02-p093-01140-r009-011",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-029",
      "parentFingerprint": "0b228a44308e56109c0faf0fbe682de0d005fb05783fb6847c91344c4acdd880",
      "passageSha256": "a902706b474b1f5980fca2b8dfe73763ebc336969975c5e805f91d5b7bb3d5a8",
      "pdfPages": [
        93
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 7,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0060",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s02-p093-01140-s010",
      "sentenceText": "Hell, if I had all this money, I’d be nice, too!”",
      "sentenceSha256": "71aa23bb7ea8f1747cbce1910e7766cdb02661116317a217f8c38b963d4da306",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s02-p093-01140-r009-011",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-029",
      "parentFingerprint": "0b228a44308e56109c0faf0fbe682de0d005fb05783fb6847c91344c4acdd880",
      "passageSha256": "a902706b474b1f5980fca2b8dfe73763ebc336969975c5e805f91d5b7bb3d5a8",
      "pdfPages": [
        93
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 8,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0061",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s03-p093-04380-s001",
      "sentenceText": "In his Critique of Judgment, Immanuel Kant distinguished beautiful arts from pleasant arts.",
      "sentenceSha256": "a1d719d816d6e9a0beb1590b81644160040f4558ff16fcb435f1c64957fa4f10",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s03-p093-04380-r001-003",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-030",
      "parentFingerprint": "c5b5e786287bfda165174ad46daf6af0464be4e452b69033c944d9cd16bbfe68",
      "passageSha256": "a92c1c0f7c3e8a0099450d1cb65bc095bbee031b9e1c847fb7d163c70ca44ce2",
      "pdfPages": [
        93
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 9,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0062",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s03-p093-04380-s004",
      "sentenceText": "In contrast, “beautiful art is a mode of representation which is purposive for itself, and which, although devoid of [definite] purpose, yet furthers the culture of the mental powers in reference to social communication.”",
      "sentenceSha256": "d0c28792e9a549ab022c4ad62d722d2a837cc58c7f6c4410d1c5f9a33d4ca1ca",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s03-p093-04380-r004-005",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-031",
      "parentFingerprint": "edd462ee60f23670cc6b33a4f869423613bf3b34c9072177a633a24dd504b261",
      "passageSha256": "7b8394ebda204fa411effa1bac45c7cf9f77c56de5cc35d8303acfb376cacfd6",
      "pdfPages": [
        93
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 10,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0063",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s03-p093-06720-s001",
      "sentenceText": "When Sonny Rollins, the legendary jazz saxophonist, was asked about art and, more specifically, why art matters, his reply evoked Kantian aesthetic judgments: “Technology is no savior.",
      "sentenceSha256": "7d1bf644cefdd7bb7ae92c6251ab5be1da7984b5a9ac538670c72b7953a06e47",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s03-p093-06720-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-032",
      "parentFingerprint": "de6a2e217ac7c377c6cb44708f08bca0d324fcb5bef91d6d773ea783ac1d9f6d",
      "passageSha256": "aa6e27a3bea7b6189bb6ae6795b17c12161b0bb803d322719e2cb4652f73a24e",
      "pdfPages": [
        93,
        94
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 11,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0064",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s03-p093-06720-s004",
      "sentenceText": "It’s infinite, and without it, the world wouldn’t exist as it does.",
      "sentenceSha256": "27c18dc159d81d7d836c152d1a73a6ec7b9a299cf96d664a68417c9bde0f6ae8",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s03-p093-06720-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-032",
      "parentFingerprint": "de6a2e217ac7c377c6cb44708f08bca0d324fcb5bef91d6d773ea783ac1d9f6d",
      "passageSha256": "aa6e27a3bea7b6189bb6ae6795b17c12161b0bb803d322719e2cb4652f73a24e",
      "pdfPages": [
        93,
        94
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 12,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0065",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s03-p093-06720-s005",
      "sentenceText": "It represents the immaterial soul: intuition, that which we feel in our hearts.",
      "sentenceSha256": "6201df90f3419892282a6ca4efe3ec97509b49cff10ba052b7b9d01177d836fe",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s03-p093-06720-r005-007",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-033",
      "parentFingerprint": "db8d1c476def28ec72c1adf44e333a99e2d6fe5a05a3175baf832609d23e2246",
      "passageSha256": "ec5c5a02d0e0544b75543f161fe6e0041d69848571615943322fafae4b22dea7",
      "pdfPages": [
        94
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 13,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0066",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s03-p093-06720-s006",
      "sentenceText": "Art matters today more than ever because it outlives the contentious political veneer that is cast over everything….",
      "sentenceSha256": "29f150b57ba8d34720a8ac4dbf2100af457d0b40b9f8e83d030a999c2b60e8de",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s03-p093-06720-r005-007",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-033",
      "parentFingerprint": "db8d1c476def28ec72c1adf44e333a99e2d6fe5a05a3175baf832609d23e2246",
      "passageSha256": "ec5c5a02d0e0544b75543f161fe6e0041d69848571615943322fafae4b22dea7",
      "pdfPages": [
        94
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 14,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0067",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s03-p094-02310-s001",
      "sentenceText": "In his essay “The Power of Art in a Political Age,” David Brooks echoes Sonny Rollins’s point.",
      "sentenceSha256": "b16502163b354b1bdc41c141b9567ebd563bf995c7c55d839c004f06ee812185",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s03-p094-02310-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-034",
      "parentFingerprint": "18de0cfa72a695263c58a092367a6bc40e85bc6c4951b69a7da5e6683c61c5b9",
      "passageSha256": "6650bb401feee6226e594bd8a45de67fd865a345cc2f370b06e4b1a7a10e61eb",
      "pdfPages": [
        94
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 15,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0068",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s03-p094-02310-s003",
      "sentenceText": "So I’m trying to take countermeasures.",
      "sentenceSha256": "8f1e2d24faec9713f5d55085703dd9c20000fcc378ace5736c26116bff3a4c06",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s03-p094-02310-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-034",
      "parentFingerprint": "18de0cfa72a695263c58a092367a6bc40e85bc6c4951b69a7da5e6683c61c5b9",
      "passageSha256": "6650bb401feee6226e594bd8a45de67fd865a345cc2f370b06e4b1a7a10e61eb",
      "pdfPages": [
        94
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 16,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0069",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s03-p094-02310-s004",
      "sentenceText": "I flee to the arts.”",
      "sentenceSha256": "9190f81f6c3df52538597ae146f3e25030aabfbd5404802f58a8eb6e50be118c",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s03-p094-02310-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-034",
      "parentFingerprint": "18de0cfa72a695263c58a092367a6bc40e85bc6c4951b69a7da5e6683c61c5b9",
      "passageSha256": "6650bb401feee6226e594bd8a45de67fd865a345cc2f370b06e4b1a7a10e61eb",
      "pdfPages": [
        94
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 17,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0070",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s03-p094-02310-s007",
      "sentenceText": "We can open ourselves up to new experiences not just through reading novels and poems, but also by looking at art.",
      "sentenceSha256": "912aa29fbee675da1738a2ea34f8723001797f7b8cc5bfa0cbfd9d6a459bc8e3",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s03-p094-02310-r005-007",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-035",
      "parentFingerprint": "db42764ef44b1ea0fedbe37fc17797257d13cf2dc17f2fb672b989edfffa0312",
      "passageSha256": "b3f3de24f9c4d916b54c62b373b228737f558841a05d056fc5ce218aafdeeb2d",
      "pdfPages": [
        94
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 18,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0071",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s03-p094-04260-s001",
      "sentenceText": "Rollins’s and Brooks’s takes on the arts remind me of Martin Heidegger’s “Das Gerede” (endless chatter).",
      "sentenceSha256": "e424203704777964ea6bc6dbf75fa22f9063124d53da6b94320e169812427dab",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s03-p094-04260-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-036",
      "parentFingerprint": "6a0c2ed88003ba23f2f063072ea1a4f6340abd95bf6fd5e83f51c497e145defa",
      "passageSha256": "1bc7a6291801025334d82822401836e438a731e6b062274c026f19f0a8de2efb",
      "pdfPages": [
        94
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 19,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0072",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s03-p094-04260-s003",
      "sentenceText": "In the world of “Das Gerede,” we understand everything without thinking deeply on our own.",
      "sentenceSha256": "8d603c0ec446d80e1bb5c57b0d770718257f9c61284c14d498f248bfe0c9443d",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s03-p094-04260-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-036",
      "parentFingerprint": "6a0c2ed88003ba23f2f063072ea1a4f6340abd95bf6fd5e83f51c497e145defa",
      "passageSha256": "1bc7a6291801025334d82822401836e438a731e6b062274c026f19f0a8de2efb",
      "pdfPages": [
        94
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 20,
      "questionId": "qe-c09-0073",
      "sentenceId": "c09-s03-p094-04260-s004",
      "sentenceText": "We are bombarded with “the constant possibility of distraction.”",
      "sentenceSha256": "d46019922028fb6ee56ea05be199aaa7b611aa1a6876a45328a42d253d94bce0",
      "readingUnitId": "c09-s03-p094-04260-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c09-036",
      "parentFingerprint": "6a0c2ed88003ba23f2f063072ea1a4f6340abd95bf6fd5e83f51c497e145defa",
      "passageSha256": "1bc7a6291801025334d82822401836e438a731e6b062274c026f19f0a8de2efb",
      "pdfPages": [
        94
